# Final Whistle — git attributes
#
# The whitespace exemption below is the load-bearing line: Unity serializes
# `.asset` / `.meta` / `.unity` / `.prefab` / `.mat` / `.controller` /
# `.shadergraph` / `.subshader` YAML with trailing spaces on blank fields
# (e.g. empty `userData: ` / `assetBundleName: ` / `m_Name: `), as a
# documented Unity convention. Functional Unity import is unaffected, but
# `git diff --check` / `git show --check` flag the trailing whitespace and
# break the repo's clean-hygiene-check habit.
#
# Codex round-5 review (2026-04-30) first caught this on the
# Addressables-init commit `0f420d7` for `.asset` / `.meta`. Codex round-1
# review against `9dc4140` (2026-04-30 Slice-2 dots-adapter scene) caught
# the same pattern on `.unity` scene files (Unity emits empty `m_Name: `
# trailing-spaces on auto-generated component sub-objects). Extending the
# exemption to ALL Unity-serialized YAML types under `unity-project/Assets/`
# pre-empts the next round catching `.prefab` / `.mat` / etc. with the
# same pattern.
#
# Setting `whitespace=-trailing-space` on Unity-generated paths exempts
# them from the trailing-space check WITHOUT disabling the check globally,
# so source files (.cs, .py, .sh, .md) still surface trailing-whitespace
# regressions normally.

# Unity-serialized YAML files everywhere they live.
unity-project/Assets/**/*.asset         whitespace=-trailing-space
unity-project/Assets/**/*.meta          whitespace=-trailing-space
unity-project/Assets/**/*.unity         whitespace=-trailing-space
unity-project/Assets/**/*.prefab        whitespace=-trailing-space
unity-project/Assets/**/*.mat           whitespace=-trailing-space
unity-project/Assets/**/*.controller    whitespace=-trailing-space
unity-project/Assets/**/*.shadergraph   whitespace=-trailing-space
unity-project/Assets/**/*.subshader     whitespace=-trailing-space
unity-project/ProjectSettings/*.asset   whitespace=-trailing-space
unity-project/ProjectSettings/*.meta    whitespace=-trailing-space
unity-project/Packages/*.json           whitespace=-trailing-space

# Treat Unity-serialized YAML as text on Windows (CRLF/LF discipline). Unity
# always writes LF; let git pass them through unchanged regardless of the
# core.autocrlf setting on the developer machine.
*.asset    text eol=lf
*.meta     text eol=lf
*.unity    text eol=lf
*.prefab   text eol=lf
*.mat      text eol=lf
*.shadergraph    text eol=lf
*.subshader      text eol=lf
*.controller     text eol=lf

# Source files under explicit LF discipline so we don't depend on per-machine
# git config. Matches the cross-platform CI matrix (ubuntu / windows / macos
# all run `bash ./scripts/fw verify` with `shell: bash`).
*.cs       text eol=lf
*.csproj   text eol=lf
*.slnx     text eol=lf
*.json     text eol=lf
*.yaml     text eol=lf
*.yml      text eol=lf
*.md       text eol=lf
*.sh       text eol=lf
*.py       text eol=lf
*.shader   text eol=lf
*.hlsl     text eol=lf
*.cginc    text eol=lf
